signature:
The Rivalry Book, built entirely on-device:
- a named roster of players with a seat picker before each one-phone game;
- a permanent match log per pair across every game, keyed by match id, with the ending (checkmate, stalemate and so on) and timestamps;
- a Rivalry detail screen with the per-game record, current and longest streaks, a last-10 form strip, and a filter by game;
- a two-phone handshake that shows 'You vs <name>' with the record before the first move, and logs the match under the shared session id on both phones;
- copy-summary and copy-CSV export.

This also fixes a real defect: today the one-phone opponent id comes from the device id (settings_service.dart:115-121), so renaming 'Second player' merges different people into one record.

Competitors were checked only through the keyless iTunes Search/Lookup API, because web search is disabled here. The listings checked were Jindoblu '2 Player Games : Offline Games' (id1465731199, 420,752 ratings), Tellmewow '2 Player Games - Pastimes' (id1496783791), CANDYBLOCKS 'Multiplayer Board Games' (id1547677867) and Plato (id1054747306). None of these listings describes two phones playing directly with no server, or a per-person history kept across many games. That is listing text only; how those apps actually behave is not verified.

must:
M2 The Rivalry Book (signature):
- roster with add, rename (history kept) and delete;
- seat picker for one-phone games;
- match log in KeyValueStore: match id, game, seats, winner or draw, ending, timestamps, one-phone or two-phone; a duplicate match id is ignored;
- migration of buddyplay.rivalries that keeps the totals exactly and invents no per-match rows;
- Rivalry detail screen: per-game table, streaks, last-10 strip, filter by game, search by name;
- 'You vs <name>' record shown when two phones connect, with both phones logging under the same session id.

M4 Real states:
- empty Rivalry Book and empty filtered views;
- host and join lobbies show a help card after 20 s with no peer (same Wi-Fi, iOS Local Network permission path, join by address, 'Play on this phone instead');
- a 'no Wi-Fi or hotspot address' message;
- corrupt history JSON shows a one-time reset notice instead of a crash.

M5 Its own identity:
- palette 'Game table' replaces every Tailwind hex in theme.dart: felt green 0xFF0E4D3A as seed and primary, brass 0xFFC9A227 accent, paper 0xFFF3EBDD light background, walnut 0xFF2B2118 dark background, seats ink navy 0xFF1F3A5F and brick 0xFFB23A48 (none of these hexes appears in any other portfolio app);
- Fraunces for display and Instrument Sans for body, bundled as OFL files (source URLs returned HTTP 200), used by no sibling app;
- 6 px 'scorecard' panels with tabular figures;
- the forced dark arenaTheme is removed (game_scaffold.dart:45) and the default theme becomes System;
- CupertinoTabBar on iOS, tabs renamed Play · Rivalry Book · Settings;
- AglAdBanner moves from the shell guard (app.dart:71) to two inline slots.

M6 Own icon and launch screen:
- a new two-pawn icon on felt with a brass ring, drawn by a BuddyPlay-specific script, never by generate_app_icons.py;
- delete the BuddyPlay row at generate_app_icons.py:65 and coordinate, since that script is shared;
- LaunchScreen.storyboard on felt green with the new mark, so its shasum is no longer 3f6a9b27…;
- matching Android splash;
- project.pbxproj is not touched.

M7 Own onboarding and Settings:
- a skippable two-step onboarding: 'Who's playing?' creates the first two roster players, then 'Same table or two phones?' explains Local Network before iOS asks;
- Settings sections become Players, At the table, Two phones and Privacy;
- remove the raw Device ID row, the 'N of M games… in this build' row and the Bluetooth notice (settings_screen.dart:135-160, 284-330).

M10 Proven:
- analyze clean, all tests passing, none deleted or skipped;
- new tests for: match-log store (idempotence, migration, rename, delete, corrupt JSON), streak maths, CSV quoting, the seat-picker regression (Sam and Alex stay separate), home truthfulness, search and count, banned phrases across lib/, theme hexes and fonts, the lobby help timeout, and trivia bank rules;
- simulator launch with screenshots attached;
- path-limited commits pushed to main, never touching fastlane/ or ios/Podfile.lock.
